(Spoilers, maybe)

I'm a semi-casual Nethack gamer. I sometimes play for awhile intensively, 
then get fed up and forget the game for months. During that I forget many 
things, but sure I also still have plenty of things to learn. One thing I 
thought I knew, but evidently didn't, is to not get cocky. I thought I was 
going to ascend with no problem... But the result was a gigantic YASD.

I usually get a spark to playing Nethack every summer vacation, when I'm 
staying at summer house. I don't have a computer there with me (wife's 
orders), but I smuggle my Nokia 9210 phone, which I use for playing Nethack. 
This summer vacation was no different. After we got back home I continued 
playing with PC, which is a lot easier due to mouse and PC keyboard. (And 
it's easier to access spoilers.)

I've only ascended once as a valkyrie, and I decided to play samurai next. 
This was my 41st try as a samurai (not counting the games I played with 
9210, can't access its log file). The game started like a nightmare - I 
bumped into a Master Mind Flayer in Gnomish mines at lvl 7. No bones file, 
and couldn't find a polymorph trap. How did that get there? A mystery. 
Anyways, the sucker almost got me, but I luckily escaped downstairs with the 
help of a teleport trap. Next level there was a cockatrice which left a 
corpse, and since I've already found gloves... Master Mind Flayer made a 
nice sculpture! I had forgot some levels and had to price-id scrolls again, 
but since it was so early in the game, it didn't really matter.

After the nightmare start, everything went like a dream. From the minetown I 
found two kinds of lamps, and later I found out that the one not flickering 
was the blessed one! I wished gray dragon scale mail. I found BoH and 
AoReflection before Sokoban, but did it anyways. Since I fumbled a boulder 
in a place I couldn't solve the final level, I had to get back to mine town 
to get a pick axe I forgot there. Once there I noticed another magic lamp in 
a general store! I saved that for a rainy day and used it as light source.

I found magic whistle relatively early, which is maybe the most helpful item 
for me after BoH. I lost quite many pets, but always found new ones. The 
longes lasting pet was a snake which hatched from an egg and mistake me for 
his daddy. I named it George W. Later it turned into umber hulk in a poly 
trap. I lost track of it during ascension run, but I suppose it survived. I 
also had so many wishes left, I used one to get a figurine of an Archon, but 
that didn't survive some of the Gehennom demons.
"You hear some noises in the distance.  "Burrrrp!""
"You have a sad feeling for a moment, then it passes."

From castle armory I found Mjollnir and Sun Sword, but didn't use them, 
instead stored them in the BoH so that my ending inventory would look 
better. After the quest and the castle I was *sure* I was going to ascend. I 
couldn't find entrance to Fort Ludios, but that didn't matter since I found 
a big leprechaun lair where I got enough money to buy some protection. After 
getting a pet Archon, she slayed the priest and I got my money back, and 
went to another priest to get more protection! After wishing for speed boots 
and gauntlets of power, a T-shirt and a magic marker, I got AC down to -40. 
I was wielding either +6 Tsurugi of Muramasa or dual wielding +7 Excalibur 
and +7 Silver saber. I had no real problems in Gehennom, and even the 
mysterious force was kind - it took me back just ONCE. Planes weren't a 
problem either, and I still had a magic lamp and wand of wishing with three 
charges (+ 1 last wrench) left, so I even spend one wish for scrolls of gold 
detection (wasn't sure if I had id'd it), so that I could find portal 
sooner. I was already thinking of my next game after the ascension, maybe a 
wizard or ranger next, and I just wanted to finish the game as soon as 
possible. I actually already started writing YAAP message!

I had three amulets of life saving when I entered astral plane, as well as 
several wands of death, plenty of food, a ring of regeneration and at least 
ten potions of full healing. I thought maybe I should put on an amulet of 
life saving and hold shield of reflection, but chose to have amulet of 
reflection and leave both hands free to hold weapon(s). I had learned from 
earlier experience and took the ring of conflict off before entering astral 
plane.

First I met a wizard wielding Magicbane. Killed it - no problem. Then came 
pestilence. I zapped two or three times with wand of death, but missed every 
time. However the wand killed all other monsters so pestilence could reach 
me. That's when it got me - I started feeling ill, very ill. I applied 
(blessed) unicorn horn, a relief, then I became more ill. Applied unicorn 
horn again. Nothing happens. And before I know it... DYWYPI?

